{
	// Cloudflare Worker config for DocMaster.
	//
	// "name" is the ONLY thing that decides whether a deploy overwrites another
	// project. It is DELIBERATELY different from the background remover
	// ("advanced-bg-remover"), so deploying DocMaster can NEVER touch or remove
	// that project. They live side by side.
	"$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
	"name": "docmaster",
	"main": "worker/index.js",
	"compatibility_date": "2026-07-21",
	"compatibility_flags": [
		"nodejs_compat"
	],
	"observability": {
		"enabled": true
	},
	// The static site built by `npm run build` (scripts/build-static.js).
	// run_worker_first: the Worker sees every request first, so it can inject the
	// per-request CSP nonce and set the isolation headers before serving assets.
	"assets": {
		"directory": "dist",
		"binding": "ASSETS",
		"run_worker_first": true
	},
	"kv_namespaces": [
		{
			"binding": "CREDITS_KV",
			"id": "ab62242a982b44c29b48e188cd998aa7",
			"remote": true
		}
	]
	// ----- Cloud AI + credits (POST /api/ai/* in worker/index.js) -----------
	// The AI proxy + per-user credit wallet live in the Worker. CREDITS_KV (the
	// wallet + audit ledger) is bound above. Remaining setup:
	//
	// 1) Set the API KEY as a SECRET (provider defaults to gemini / gemini-3.6-flash):
	//      npx wrangler secret put AI_API_KEY
	//    Optional — pick another provider/model with plain vars:
	//      // "vars": { "AI_PROVIDER": "gemini", "AI_MODEL": "gemini-3.6-flash" },
	//    (Supabase URL + anon key have safe public defaults in worker/auth.js;
	//     override with SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY vars only if the project moves.)
	//
	// 2) OPTIONAL — view usage at /admin/usage (per-user credits/tokens/cost):
	//      npx wrangler secret put ADMIN_TOKEN
	//    then open https://<your-domain>/admin/usage?token=YOUR_TOKEN
	//
	// Without AI_API_KEY, /api/ai/chat returns 503 (feature off). Without CREDITS_KV
	// the AI still answers but balances won't persist (no real metering).
	// ----- Contact form (POST /api/contact in worker/index.js) --------------
	// Messages are STORED in KV (browse them under Workers & Pages → KV in the
	// dashboard) and, if a mail provider is set, EMAILED to your inbox.
	//
	// 1) To store in KV, create a namespace and uncomment the binding below:
	//      npx wrangler kv namespace create CONTACT_KV
	//    then paste the printed id here (add a comma after the assets block) and
	//    redeploy:
	//      "kv_namespaces": [
	//        { "binding": "CONTACT_KV", "id": "<your-kv-namespace-id>" }
	//      ]
	//
	// 2) To EMAIL every message to your inbox (easiest — no domain/DNS needed),
	//    get a free access key at https://web3forms.com and set it as a secret:
	//      npx wrangler secret put WEB3FORMS_KEY
	//      npx wrangler secret put CONTACT_TO      # optional: your inbox address
	//    (Alternatively use Resend: set RESEND_API_KEY and optionally RESEND_FROM.)
	//    Secrets are set on the deployed Worker — never in this file or the client.
	// The oversized AI files (the 59 MB ONNX layout model + the 26 MB ORT .wasm)
	// exceed Cloudflare's 25 MiB asset limit, so they are NOT bundled here. They
	// are published on this repo's GitHub Release and the Worker proxies them
	// same-origin (see RELEASE_BASE in worker/index.js). No R2, no bucket, no card.
}